# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CODEOWNERS — Gate 1 of the delivery pipeline
#
# Every rule here becomes a MANDATORY reviewer on any PR touching the matched
# paths, provided "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in branch
# protection. See docs/CI-CD.md and scripts/bootstrap-governance.sh.
#
# Last match wins. Order is therefore significant — the most specific rule for a
# path must appear last.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !! IMPORTANT — TEAM HANDLES ARE PLACEHOLDERS !!
#
# The programme roster in docs/requirements/index.md identifies people by
# Confluence handle (@shubham.mujumdar1 … @shubham.mujumdar10). Those are NOT
# GitHub accounts. GitHub SILENTLY IGNORES a CODEOWNERS entry naming a user or
# team that does not exist or lacks write access to this repository — the file
# stays "valid" and the gate simply never fires.
#
# So this file uses GitHub *team* slugs, which must be created in the
# organisation and populated with the corresponding people before Gate 1 is
# real. The mapping is below. Verify with:
#     Repo → Settings → Branches → CODEOWNERS errors
#
# GitHub team                        Roster handle        Role
# ---------------------------------  -------------------  -------------------------------
# @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads    @shubham.mujumdar4   Engineering Lead — Payments
# @cognizantfs/payments-architects   @shubham.mujumdar3   Solution Architect / DA chair
# @cognizantfs/payments-qa           @shubham.mujumdar6   QA Lead
# @cognizantfs/payments-compliance   @shubham.mujumdar7   Compliance & Financial Crime Risk
# @cognizantfs/payments-sre          @shubham.mujumdar9   SRE / Platform Engineering
# @cognizantfs/payments-product      @shubham.mujumdar1   Product Owner / Lead BA
