# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Default owner -----------------------------------------------------------
# The Engineering Lead is accountable for code review standards across the
# repository (roster: "code review standards").
*                                   @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads


# --- Design Authority scope --------------------------------------------------
# The Solution Architect chairs the DA, which owns architectural decisions and
# NFRs. These paths are the seams ARCHITECTURE.md section 10 calls out as load
# bearing: changing them changes the shape of the system, not just its detail.
/src/main/java/com/poc/paymentprocessing/gateway/    @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-architects
/src/main/java/com/poc/paymentprocessing/service/    @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-architects
/src/main/java/com/poc/paymentprocessing/entity/     @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-architects
/pom.xml                                             @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-architects


# --- Compliance scope --------------------------------------------------------
# The audit trail is the compliance control evidence for this service, and the
# exception handler decides what leaves the system boundary on a failure.
# Configuration is here because it governs whether the H2 console is exposed
# (SPEC.md section 6.11).
/src/main/java/com/poc/paymentprocessing/service/PaymentAuditService.java   @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-compliance
/src/main/java/com/poc/paymentprocessing/exception/                        @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-compliance
/src/main/resources/                                                       @cognizantfs/payments-eng-leads @cognizantfs/payments-compliance


# --- Quality scope -----------------------------------------------------------
# The QA Lead owns RTM-30, the test strategy and coverage reporting, so test
# changes — especially ones that would weaken a gate — need their review.
/src/test/                          @cognizantfs/payments-qa


# --- Platform scope ----------------------------------------------------------
# SRE owns deployment and observability. Note this deliberately does NOT include
# the eng-leads team: a developer must not be able to approve a change that
# relaxes the pipeline's own gates.
/.github/workflows/                 @cognizantfs/payments-sre @cognizantfs/payments-architects
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @cognizantfs/payments-sre @cognizantfs/payments-delivery
/Dockerfile                         @cognizantfs/payments-sre
